  "limitations": [
    "Predicted binding only. No processing, presentation, immunogenicity or T-cell measurement, and no experimental validation of any peptide.",
    "MHCflurry percentile ranks are internal to the pinned model bundle. They normalise its nM scale across alleles; they are not measured ligand yields, and the 0.5 and 2 percent thresholds are NetMHCpan conventions applied to a different predictor whose reference distribution is its own.",
    "Rank normalisation assumes each allele presents a comparable share of the peptide universe. Real repertoire breadth differs between alleles, so part of the nM offset may be biological rather than a scale artefact.",
    "No single scale is uniquely allele-neutral. The geometric mean used here is a choice, and the resulting order is not invariant to it.",
    "HLA-C down-weighting uses published ratios from normal lymphocytes of a different haplotype. Allele-specific surface density was not measured for Yash, and the bundled vendor expression is gene-level RNA, neither allele-resolved nor a surface-protein measurement.",
    "HLA loss of heterozygosity was not assayed. Haplotype-loss rows enumerate the four possible A/B/C phasings of the recorded alleles as hypotheses.",
    "Crossing a gate removes a region from a count, not its peptides. Next-best affinities and percentiles are in single-allele-dependence.tsv.",
    "Target peptide sets, flanks, the 25-aa windows and the expression proxies are the recorded ones; only the per-allele nM scale and the HLA-C weight are varied."
  ]
}
